*.swo

# Hub SPA node deps (QUM-878). The generated web/gen bindings and the built
# cmd/hubd/web/dist ARE committed (so `make validate`/`go build` stay node-free);
# only the installed node_modules is ignored.
web/node_modules/
web/*.tsbuildinfo

# Sprawl runtime state (config.yaml is tracked, everything else is ignored)
.sprawl/*
!.sprawl/config.yaml

# Agent findings dirs (QUM-989). The SANCTIONED location for agent artifacts is
# .sprawl/agents/<name>/findings/, already covered by `.sprawl/*` above — but an
# agent that drops a findings/ dir anywhere ELSE was covered by nothing. That is
# the same shape as the tfplan gap: a sensitive-by-default class that no pattern
# happened to match. Measured, not hypothetical — across 94 agent branches the
# only two carrying genuinely unmerged content carried nothing BUT a top-level
# findings/ dir (9 and 3 files), while 9 further worktrees had the same class of
# artifact sitting untracked in the same place. Same files, same path; whether
# they got committed turned purely on whether an agent happened to run git add.
#
# UNANCHORED on purpose — agents work in worktrees and create findings/ at
# whatever depth they are standing in, so `/findings/` would cover the least
# likely case. `sprawl` at the top of this file is the existing precedent for
# the unanchored form here.
#
# COST, recorded: a legitimately tracked findings/ dir ANYWHERE in the tree now
# needs `git add -f`. Nothing is tracked under such a path today (verified), and
# per CLAUDE.md the sanctioned home for these artifacts is gitignored anyway.
# This is a directory pattern, so it does not match a mere substring —
# docs/findings-summary.md stays stageable.
findings/

.claude/settings.local.json
.codex
CLAUDE.local.md

# Local secrets (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, etc.) — see CLAUDE.md
.env

# Terraform / IaC (QUM-870) — nothing instance-specific or stateful enters the tree.
# Real values live ONLY in gitignored tfvars / backend-config / .env; committed IaC
# is fully parameterized. .terraform.lock.hcl is intentionally NOT ignored (tracked).
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
backend-config*.hcl
# Plan output (QUM-989) — a rendered diff of live infrastructure: resource
# names, IDs, and often secret values in plaintext. `tfplan*` and `*.tfplan`
# are both needed (`tfplan5` vs `terraform.tfplan`); deliberately unanchored,
# because terraform is run from deploy/hub/infra/terraform/azure/, not the root.
tfplan*
*.tfplan
plan.out
# `plan.out` is an exact basename, so `apply.out` / `terraform-plan.out` and
# the `terraform show -json` renderings (`plan.out.json`, `*.tfplan.json`) are
# knowingly NOT covered here — they are left to review rather than silently
# widened beyond what QUM-989 measured. Tracked as QUM-994.

# az / credential scratch produced during bootstrap
*.azcreds
az-scratch/
bootstrap.env

# Tool/build/apply logs (QUM-989). Deliberately BROAD. `terraform apply` and
# `az acr build` emit ad-hoc logs (apply4.log, acrbuild2.log) whose names nobody
# can enumerate in advance, and this repo is PUBLIC — such logs routinely carry
# resource IDs, FQDNs, and employer-internal specifics. The content guard
# (scripts/guard-employer-leak) is text-only and blind to binaries, so for the
# artifact classes in QUM-989 this ignore rule is the only defence, not one
# layer of several.
#
# TRADE-OFF, recorded on purpose: broad costs DETECTABILITY, on TWO discovery
# paths, not one — `git status` will no longer surface a stray *.log, and
# `git clean -nd` will not list it either (that needs -x). A stray *.log
# appearing in a worktree is exactly how QUM-989 was found, and QUM-989's item
# 4 (identify the writer) is closed as unresolvable, so if that writer runs
# again we will not notice. We chose staging-safety anyway because the failure
# modes are asymmetric: an unnoticed ignored log is a non-event, an unnoticed
# COMMITTED log is a public leak.
#
# What makes the trade acceptable is the companion rule in CLAUDE.md ("Never
# `git add -A`"). Staging an ignored path EXPLICITLY fails loudly — git refuses
# with "The following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files" — so
# under explicit-path staging a legitimate log can never be silently dropped,
# only loudly refused. Broad ignores and explicit-path staging reinforce each
# other; broad ignores plus `-A` would not. A log you genuinely want tracked
# must be `git add -f`'d and negated below.
*.log
# The one intentionally tracked log (sanitized research evidence). gitignore
# does not affect already-tracked files, so this negation is documentation of
# intent plus a guarantee that a future re-add still works. It must stay AFTER
# `*.log` — last matching pattern wins.
!docs/research/m13-phase1-evidence/ec6-live-handoff-stderr.log

# QUM-871 spike client evidence logs — timestamped run output; may reference the
# live FQDN, so gitignored. The dir is kept via .gitkeep.
deploy/hub/spike/logs/*
!deploy/hub/spike/logs/.gitkeep
# Operator runbooks that may reference corporate specifics — gitignored.
# Committed docs are the sanitized README.md; *.local.md stays out of the tree.
deploy/hub/**/*.local.md
